<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Belém</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1616">1616</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Belém do Pará</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Belém is a port city near the mouth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amazon">Amazon</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a> and the capital of the state of Pará. The Portuguese founded it in 1616 as the fort of Presépio to secure the river against French, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> and English rivals. It became the capital of the State of Grão-Pará and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maranhao">Maranhão</a> in 1751, a centre of the Cabanagem revolt of 1835, and grew rich during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rubber">rubber</a> boom of the late nineteenth century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/belem.jpg" alt="Belém" width="320" height="114" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Burn86 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:L1010748-L1010765_copie_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
